⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
295 calories 24g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins included)

Reese’s Caramel Craze Protein Blizzard 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 140 recipes like this one!

- 400g Fat Free @fairlife Milk
- 40-45g @Lakanto Monk Fruit sweetener
- 5g (1 tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
- A pinch of salt
Mix-ins:
- 10g Mini @Reeses PB Cups
- 12g (2 pieces) Mini Rolos (or any chocolate covered caramels)
- 10g chocolate chips mixed with 1.5g of coconut oil
• Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 10g of chocolate with 1.5g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips.
295 cal 30g C, 10g F, 24g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting if powdery
5. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the melted chocolate, chopped PB cups, and chopped Rolos
6. Run the “Mix-in” cycle

